From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: allolive <160342668+allolive@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 04:47:37 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] Blu-ray 3D: play the base view alone when its second view
 cannot be read

An extension file that could not be opened turned 3D off at once, but
the video stream stayed set up for MVC, with the MVC codec tag and the
extension's header appended to its own. The base view then went to an
MVC decoder alone, and the AML MVC decoder outputs a picture only when
both views arrive: the picture froze for the rest of the playlist.

A failed open, whatever the reason (an I/O error, a file the share does
not show during an outage, a file without an MVC stream), is now tried
again as the base view reads on, every half second of it, opening the
extension at the oldest base picture still waiting. Every wait is
measured on the base view's newest picture, which does not move on while
its share is away, so an outage costs nothing. A failed open more than
five seconds of the base view past the last pair ends the extension for
the playlist; so does a move of the extension more than 16 s past it,
which ends an extension that opens and reads but never pairs after three
moves or so. An open at the end of the extension's play item that fails
is tried again the same way. A play item the playlist's sub-path does
not have still ends the extension at once.

Ending the extension for the playlist leaves the playlist's timestamps
and clip joins as for 3D, since switching them in the middle of the
playlist would step every stream's clock; disabling it for the disc,
when the video decoder cannot decode MVC, stays as it was. The base
pictures waiting for their second view are dropped, rather than handed
to a decoder that could start from few of them, and the video stream is
set up again for the base view alone, with the codec tag and header
ffmpeg's stream still has. Its change count moves on, so the player
opens the decoder again as plain H.264, which starts at the next
sequence header, key picture or recovery point: the picture stays frozen
from the last pair through the 5 s of retries and up to a GOP more. The
stream stays 2D until the next playlist.

When a demuxer first sets the video stream up and the extension cannot
be opened for it, the extension ends for the playlist at once, whatever
the reason, even an outage that would have passed: the stream cannot be
set up for MVC without the extension's header, and is not set up again
from 2D to 3D in the middle of a playlist. A later setup, on a change of
picture size while the extension is being tried again, keeps the stream
set up for MVC with the header of the extension last opened, stale
should a later clip's second view carry another one, and leaves the
extension to those tries.

Once a Blu-ray's video stream has been set up with its second view from
the extension's file, a later setup no longer looks for an MVC stream in
the base view's own transport stream: with the extension ended, a base
view file that also carries one would have set the stream up for MVC
again, which the check for an ended extension then undid, on every
packet. A Blu-ray without an extension file, with its second view in the
base view's transport stream, is set up from that as before.

Shared code, unavoidable: the 3D Blu-ray demuxer exists only in
CoreELEC's Kodi (DVDInputStreamBluray, CDemuxMVC, CDemuxStreamSSIF and
their use in DVDDemuxFFmpeg) and has no AML counterpart.

Signed-off-by: allolive <160342668+allolive@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 .../DVDDemuxers/DVDDemuxFFmpeg.cpp            | 56 +++++++++++++------
 .../DVDDemuxers/DemuxStreamSSIF.cpp           | 44 +++++++++++++--
 .../VideoPlayer/DVDDemuxers/DemuxStreamSSIF.h | 11 ++++
 .../DVDInputStreams/DVDInputStream.h          |  2 +
 .../DVDInputStreams/DVDInputStreamBluray.cpp  | 17 +++++-
 .../DVDInputStreams/DVDInputStreamBluray.h    |  1 +
 6 files changed, 107 insertions(+), 24 deletions(-)

diff --git a/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/DVDDemuxers/DVDDemuxFFmpeg.cpp b/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/DVDDemuxers/DVDDemuxFFmpeg.cpp
index 80d5b40..be90806 100644
--- a/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/DVDDemuxers/DVDDemuxFFmpeg.cpp
+++ b/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/DVDDemuxers/DVDDemuxFFmpeg.cpp
@@ -47,6 +47,7 @@
 #include <map>
 #include <memory>
 #include <mutex>
+#include <span>
 #include <sstream>
 #include <tuple>
 #include <utility>
@@ -1466,6 +1467,10 @@ DemuxPacket* CDVDDemuxFFmpeg::ReadInternal(bool keep)
         // content has changed
         stream = AddStream(pPacket->iStreamId);
       }
+      // a Blu-ray's second view was turned off: the stream is set up again for the base view alone
+      else if (stream->codec_fourcc == FOURCC_AMVC && m_pSSIF && m_pSSIF->IsBluRay() &&
+               !m_pSSIF->HasExtention())
+        stream = AddStream(pPacket->iStreamId);
       if (stream && stream->codec == AV_CODEC_ID_H264)
         pPacket->recoveryPoint = m_seekToKeyFrame;
       m_seekToKeyFrame = false;
@@ -2068,7 +2073,8 @@ CDemuxStream* CDVDDemuxFFmpeg::AddStream(int streamIdx)
     }
 
     CDemuxStream* stream = nullptr;
-    const AVStream* mvcStream = nullptr;
+    bool mvc = false;
+    std::span<const uint8_t> mvcHeader;
 
     switch (pStream->codecpar->codec_type)
     {
@@ -2474,11 +2480,15 @@ CDemuxStream* CDVDDemuxFFmpeg::AddStream(int streamIdx)
                 baseView ? std::dynamic_pointer_cast<CDVDInputStream::IExtentionStream>(m_pInput)
                          : nullptr;
 
-            // the extension is opened for the stream it goes with
-            if (pExt && pExt->HasExtention() && !pExt->GetExtentionDemux())
-              pExt->OpenNextStream();
+            // the extension is opened for the stream it goes with. Without it a first setup is 2D,
+            // and stays so until the next playlist; a later one keeps the header of the extension
+            // last opened, which the pairing tries to open again
+            const bool wasBlurayMvc = m_pSSIF && m_pSSIF->IsBluRay();
+            if (pExt && pExt->HasExtention() && !pExt->GetExtentionDemux() &&
+                !pExt->OpenNextStream() && !wasBlurayMvc)
+              pExt->EndExtention();
 
-            if (pExt && pExt->HasExtention() && pExt->GetExtentionDemux())
+            if (pExt && pExt->HasExtention() && (pExt->GetExtentionDemux() || wasBlurayMvc))
             {
               // a stream change keeps the dependent view already read ahead for the base view
               if (!m_pSSIF)
@@ -2490,13 +2500,24 @@ CDemuxStream* CDVDDemuxFFmpeg::AddStream(int streamIdx)
 
               st->stereo_mode = pExt && pExt->AreEyesFlipped() ? "block_rl" : "block_lr";
 
-              const std::shared_ptr<CDVDInputStream::IMenus> menuInterface =
-                  std::dynamic_pointer_cast<CDVDInputStream::IMenus>(m_pInput);
-              CDemuxMVC *extDemux = pExt->GetExtentionDemux();
-              extDemux->SetStartTime(m_pFormatContext->start_time, menuInterface->GetSupportedMenuType());
-              mvcStream = extDemux->GetAVStream();
+              CDemuxMVC* extDemux = pExt->GetExtentionDemux();
+              if (extDemux)
+              {
+                const std::shared_ptr<CDVDInputStream::IMenus> menuInterface =
+                    std::dynamic_pointer_cast<CDVDInputStream::IMenus>(m_pInput);
+                extDemux->SetStartTime(m_pFormatContext->start_time,
+                                       menuInterface->GetSupportedMenuType());
+                const AVCodecParameters* codecpar = extDemux->GetAVStream()->codecpar;
+                mvcHeader = {codecpar->extradata, static_cast<size_t>(codecpar->extradata_size)};
+                m_pSSIF->SetMVCHeader(codecpar->extradata, codecpar->extradata_size);
+              }
+              else
+                mvcHeader = m_pSSIF->GetMVCHeader();
+              mvc = true;
             }
-            else if (CDVDCodecUtils::GetH264MvcStreamIndex(m_pFormatContext, &mvcIndex))
+            // a Blu-ray's second view set up from its own file is not looked for in the base view's
+            else if (!wasBlurayMvc &&
+                     CDVDCodecUtils::GetH264MvcStreamIndex(m_pFormatContext, &mvcIndex))
             {
               if (!m_pSSIF)
                 m_pSSIF = new CDemuxStreamSSIF();
@@ -2505,7 +2526,9 @@ CDemuxStream* CDVDDemuxFFmpeg::AddStream(int streamIdx)
 
               // use lr if we don't know what the stereo mode is
               st->stereo_mode = stereoMode.empty() ? "block_lr" : stereoMode;
-              mvcStream = m_pFormatContext->streams[m_pSSIF->GetMVCStreamId()];
+              const AVCodecParameters* codecpar = m_pFormatContext->streams[mvcIndex]->codecpar;
+              mvcHeader = {codecpar->extradata, static_cast<size_t>(codecpar->extradata_size)};
+              mvc = true;
             }
           }
           else if (CDVDCodecUtils::ProcessH264MVCExtradata(pStream->codecpar->extradata, pStream->codecpar->extradata_size))
@@ -2694,16 +2717,15 @@ CDemuxStream* CDVDDemuxFFmpeg::AddStream(int streamIdx)
     }
 
     // ffmpeg's stream keeps the base view's tag and header, which a setup for it alone starts from
-    if (mvcStream)
+    if (mvc)
     {
       stream->codec_fourcc = FOURCC_AMVC;
       const size_t size = stream->extraData.GetSize();
-      if (size > 0 && mvcStream->codecpar->extradata_size > 0)
+      if (size > 0 && !mvcHeader.empty())
       {
-        FFmpegExtraData extraData(size + mvcStream->codecpar->extradata_size);
+        FFmpegExtraData extraData(size + mvcHeader.size());
         memcpy(extraData.GetData(), stream->extraData.GetData(), size);
-        memcpy(extraData.GetData() + size, mvcStream->codecpar->extradata,
-               mvcStream->codecpar->extradata_size);
+        memcpy(extraData.GetData() + size, mvcHeader.data(), mvcHeader.size());
         stream->extraData = std::move(extraData);
       }
     }
diff --git a/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/DVDDemuxers/DemuxStreamSSIF.cpp b/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/DVDDemuxers/DemuxStreamSSIF.cpp
index b347746..52e8035 100644
--- a/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/DVDDemuxers/DemuxStreamSSIF.cpp
+++ b/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/DVDDemuxers/DemuxStreamSSIF.cpp
@@ -33,6 +33,8 @@
 #define H264_QUEUE_MAX 512
 #define MVC_RETRY_SPAN (DVD_TIME_BASE / 2)
 #define MVC_DROP_MAX 512
+#define MVC_OPEN_MAX (5 * DVD_TIME_BASE)
+#define MVC_RESYNC_MAX (16 * DVD_TIME_BASE)
 
 static double Timestamp(const DemuxPacket* pkt)
 {
@@ -48,7 +50,12 @@ DemuxPacket* CDemuxStreamSSIF::AddPacket(DemuxPacket*& srcPkt, int playItem)
   if (srcPkt->iStreamId == m_h264StreamId)
   {
     if (m_bluRay && !m_bluRay->HasExtention())
+    {
+      // the extension was turned off while base pictures waited for it
+      if (!m_H264queue.empty() || !m_MVCqueue.empty())
+        Flush();
       return srcPkt;
+    }
 #if defined(DEBUG_VERBOSE)
     CLog::Log(LOGDEBUG, ">>> MVC add h264 packet: pts: {:.3f} dts: {:.3f}", srcPkt->pts*1e-6, srcPkt->dts*1e-6);
 #endif
@@ -163,11 +170,28 @@ void CDemuxStreamSSIF::Resync(double ts, int playItem, const char* reason)
   if (m_resyncTime != DVD_NOPTS_VALUE && std::abs(newest - m_resyncTime) < MVC_WAIT_MAX)
     return;
 
+  FlushMVC();
+  // moves that lead to no pair end the extension
+  if (std::abs(newest - m_pairTime) > MVC_RESYNC_MAX)
+  {
+    m_bluRay->EndExtention();
+    return;
+  }
   CLog::Log(LOGWARNING, "CDemuxStreamSSIF - {}, moving the second view to {:.3f}", reason,
             ts / DVD_TIME_BASE);
-  FlushMVC();
   m_resyncTime = newest;
   m_bluRay->ResyncExtention(ts, playItem);
+  if (!m_bluRay->GetExtentionDemux())
+    OpenFailed(newest);
+}
+
+// A failed open is tried again as the base view reads on, which it does not while its source
+// stalls; for so long only past the last pair.
+void CDemuxStreamSSIF::OpenFailed(double newest)
+{
+  m_retryTime = newest;
+  if (std::abs(newest - m_pairTime) > MVC_OPEN_MAX)
+    m_bluRay->EndExtention();
 }
 
 DemuxPacket* CDemuxStreamSSIF::MergePacket(DemuxPacket* &srcPkt, DemuxPacket* &appendPkt)
@@ -319,7 +343,7 @@ bool CDemuxStreamSSIF::FillMVCQueue(double tsBase)
   if (!m_bluRay)
     return false;
 
-  // after a failed read the extension is read again once the base view has moved on a little
+  // after a failed read or open the extension is tried again once the base view has moved on
   const double newest = Timestamp(m_H264queue.back());
   if (m_retryTime != DVD_NOPTS_VALUE && std::abs(newest - m_retryTime) < MVC_RETRY_SPAN)
     return false;
@@ -327,7 +351,16 @@ bool CDemuxStreamSSIF::FillMVCQueue(double tsBase)
 
   CDemuxMVC* demux = m_bluRay->GetExtentionDemux();
   if (!demux)
-    return false;
+  {
+    // opened at the oldest base picture waiting for it
+    m_bluRay->ResyncExtention(tsBase, FrontPlayItem());
+    demux = m_bluRay->GetExtentionDemux();
+    if (!demux)
+    {
+      OpenFailed(newest);
+      return false;
+    }
+  }
 
   DemuxPacket* mvc;
   int dropped = 0;
@@ -353,7 +386,10 @@ bool CDemuxStreamSSIF::FillMVCQueue(double tsBase)
   };
   // only the end of the file moves the extension to the next clip
   if (m_MVCqueue.size() != MVC_QUEUE_SIZE && demux->IsEOF())
-    m_bluRay->OpenNextStream();
+  {
+    if (!m_bluRay->OpenNextStream() && !m_bluRay->GetExtentionDemux())
+      OpenFailed(newest);
+  }
   else if (m_MVCqueue.empty())
     m_retryTime = newest;
 
diff --git a/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/DVDDemuxers/DemuxStreamSSIF.h b/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/DVDDemuxers/DemuxStreamSSIF.h
index 52b6bc3..e6a8fe4 100644
--- a/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/DVDDemuxers/DemuxStreamSSIF.h
+++ b/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/DVDDemuxers/DemuxStreamSSIF.h
@@ -25,8 +25,10 @@
 #endif
 #include "DVDInputStreams/DVDInputStream.h"
 #include "cores/VideoPlayer/Interface/TimingConstants.h"
+#include <algorithm>
 #include <deque>
 #include <queue>
+#include <vector>
 
 extern "C" {
 #include "libavformat/avformat.h"
@@ -48,6 +50,13 @@ public:
   void AddMVCExtPacket(DemuxPacket* &scrPkt);
   void SetBluRay(const std::shared_ptr<CDVDInputStream::IExtentionStream> &bluRay) { m_bluRay = bluRay; };
   bool IsBluRay() { return m_bluRay != nullptr; };
+  bool HasExtention() const { return m_bluRay && m_bluRay->HasExtention(); }
+  //! the second view's header, kept for a setup while the extension is not open
+  void SetMVCHeader(const uint8_t* data, int size)
+  {
+    m_mvcHeader.assign(data, data + std::max(size, 0));
+  }
+  const std::vector<uint8_t>& GetMVCHeader() const { return m_mvcHeader; }
 
 private:
   DemuxPacket* GetMVCPacket();
@@ -57,6 +66,7 @@ private:
   void DropUnpairedBase();
   void Resync(double ts, int playItem, const char* reason);
   int FrontPlayItem();
+  void OpenFailed(double newest);
 
   std::shared_ptr<CDVDInputStream::IExtentionStream> m_bluRay = nullptr;
   std::queue<DemuxPacket*> m_H264queue;
@@ -76,4 +86,5 @@ private:
   //! the play item of the base pictures queued: the number of the first of each run, and the item
   std::deque<std::pair<uint64_t, int>> m_playItems;
   uint64_t m_basePushed = 0;
+  std::vector<uint8_t> m_mvcHeader;
 };
diff --git a/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/DVDInputStreams/DVDInputStream.h b/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/DVDInputStreams/DVDInputStream.h
index 3ded7e4..ec1d04c 100644
--- a/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/DVDInputStreams/DVDInputStream.h
+++ b/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/DVDInputStreams/DVDInputStream.h
@@ -167,6 +167,8 @@ public:
     virtual bool AreEyesFlipped() = 0;
     virtual CDemuxMVC* GetExtentionDemux() = 0;
     virtual void DisableExtention() = 0;
+    //! turn the extension off until the next playlist; the base view keeps its timestamps
+    virtual void EndExtention() = 0;
     virtual bool OpenNextStream() = 0;
     //! move the extension to the base view's picture at ts, as the extension demuxer converts it,
     //! read in playItem (-1 if unknown)
diff --git a/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/DVDInputStreams/DVDInputStreamBluray.cpp b/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/DVDInputStreams/DVDInputStreamBluray.cpp
index 0154e3c..582aa1d 100644
--- a/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/DVDInputStreams/DVDInputStreamBluray.cpp
+++ b/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/DVDInputStreams/DVDInputStreamBluray.cpp
@@ -721,6 +721,18 @@ void CDVDInputStreamBluray::DisableExtention()
   m_hasMVCExtension = false;
 }
 
+// m_hasMVCExtension stays: the timestamps of the playlist and its clip joins go on as for 3D
+void CDVDInputStreamBluray::EndExtention()
+{
+  if (!m_bMVCPlayback)
+    return;
+
+  CLog::Log(LOGWARNING, "CDVDInputStreamBluray - the MVC extension cannot be read, playing the "
+                        "base view only until the next playlist");
+  CloseMVCDemux();
+  m_bMVCPlayback = false;
+}
+
 int CDVDInputStreamBluray::Read(uint8_t* buf, int buf_size)
 {
   int result = 0;
@@ -1620,7 +1632,7 @@ bool CDVDInputStreamBluray::OpenMVCDemux(int playItem)
   if (!pl || !ClipAt(playItem) || m_nMVCSubPathIndex >= pl->ext_sub_count ||
       playItem >= pl->ext_sub_path[m_nMVCSubPathIndex].sub_playitem_count)
   {
-    m_bMVCPlayback = false;
+    EndExtention();
     return false;
   }
 
@@ -1642,10 +1654,10 @@ bool CDVDInputStreamBluray::OpenMVCDemux(int playItem)
     m_pMVCInput = input;
   }
 
+  // a file that cannot be opened is tried again as the base view reads on (CDemuxStreamSSIF)
   if (!m_pMVCInput->Open())
   {
     CloseMVCDemux();
-    m_bMVCPlayback = false;
     return false;
   }
 
@@ -1654,7 +1666,6 @@ bool CDVDInputStreamBluray::OpenMVCDemux(int playItem)
   if (!m_pMVCDemux->Open(m_pMVCInput))
   {
     CloseMVCDemux();
-    m_bMVCPlayback = false;
     return false;
   }
 
diff --git a/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/DVDInputStreams/DVDInputStreamBluray.h b/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/DVDInputStreams/DVDInputStreamBluray.h
index ecf7baa..d3189fa 100644
--- a/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/DVDInputStreams/DVDInputStreamBluray.h
+++ b/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/DVDInputStreams/DVDInputStreamBluray.h
@@ -185,6 +185,7 @@ public:
   bool HasExtention() override { return m_bMVCPlayback; }
   bool AreEyesFlipped() override { return m_bFlipEyes; }
   void DisableExtention() override;
+  void EndExtention() override;
   bool OpenNextStream() override;
   void ResyncExtention(double ts, int playItem) override;
   bool IsExtentionAtStart(int playItem) override;
